[# docs-src/repos/cx-platform-fabric.cxd — the fabric's page,
   repo-cx-platform-fabric.html (RULED: DOCS-41, DOCS-47, DOCS-49 wave 3).
   Facts from the registries; the one example from its own corpus (the
   fabric suite). #]

[repo name=cx-platform-fabric
  [intro
    """Messaging with the durability written on it. `cx-platform-fabric`
       is publish/subscribe and request/reply over the primitives this site
       already ships: the durable plane rides the [[store]]'s journal — a
       published event is appended to a named stream, attributed, in a
       per-stream total order on a hash chain — and the transient plane is
       an emit whose latest value wins. A subscription says which plane it
       reads from, so nothing is at-least-once by accident."""]
  [body
    """A subscription carries a pattern and, when it names a group, an
       offset: receive a batch, `ack` it, and a second subscriber in the same
       group resumes after the acknowledged sequence — the corpus opens a
       fresh subscription to prove it. An observer with no group cannot
       acknowledge, an ungrouped `ack` is refused, and an uncommitted tail is
       redelivered. The offset is store data, readable by the same query
       verbs as anything else in the journal."""]
  [body
    """Poison is a policy, not a surprise: a dead-letter rule names the
       stream, the group and the attempt count, a message that keeps failing
       is moved to the dead-letter stream in an envelope that says why, and
       the group unblocks; a rule that would loop a stream into itself is
       refused when it is declared. Request/reply registers a responder and
       answers a synchronous call, or an error when no responder is
       registered. The same handle opens embedded over a journal element or
       remote over `xsp://`, where the dial needs the `net` grant and a
       tenant, and `fabric-serve` is the daemon on the other end."""]
  [gives
    """One module of the platform group, the whole surface — open, publish,
       subscribe, receive, ack, emit, read, respond, request — linking to the
       reference page projected from its own documentation."""]
  [try
    """One durable publish to `orders`, then a subscription on a glob pattern
       over the same stream and a batched receive: one event, matched by its
       pattern, from an in-memory journal that needed no grant."""]
  [fixture id=fabric-004-subscribe-glob-receive]
  [status
    """The fabric builds on the store, identity, the wire and the session
       layer, and is built on by the application host; the front door
       compiles its V module from the pin, and the module's own
       initialisation registers `fabric-serve` as a verb of the binary."""]]
